{
  "$comment": "Pit Planner cooking rules. Times are minutes at a 225F pit unless noted. 'pit' means the smoker set point chosen on the Plan screen. Rates are planning estimates, not doneness: probe temp and tenderness decide when food is done.",
  "version": 1,
  "tempModel": {
    "$comment": "Cook time multiplier vs 225F: factor = base ^ ((T - 225) / 25). 0.85 per 25F fits the published 225/250/275 rates. Outside trustedRange the app shows a warning instead of a confident time.",
    "referenceF": 225,
    "basePer25F": 0.85,
    "trustedRangeF": [200, 300]
  },
  "learning": {
    "$comment": "Learned rate = (priorWeight * default + sum of observed rates normalized to 225F) / (priorWeight + n). Size-adjusted timing (time ~ weight^sizeExponent, anchored to the hr/lb rate at the food's reference weight) is open from the first cook; learning refines it. A saved rate is used as-is until savedRateLearnsAfter logged cooks, then it becomes the prior the cooks blend with, unless the user locks it. rateHint: soft warning when a user rate is outside this range (hr/lb at 225F).",
    "priorWeight": 3,
    "savedRateLearnsAfter": 3, "rateHint": [0.5, 1.6], "rateLimits": [0.3, 2.5],
    "sizeExponent": 0.67
  },
